      "message": "Cherry pick is not clean. These are the differences between the original change and this cherry-pick:\nChecked against UPSTREAM commit: [googlesource](https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/b4060db9251f919506e4d672737c6b8ab9a84701) [kernel.org](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003db4060db9251f919506e4d672737c6b8ab9a84701)\n\n```\n      ## drivers/base/power/runtime.c ##\n     @@ drivers/base/power/runtime.c: EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pm_runtime_enable);\n    @@ drivers/base/power/runtime.c: EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(pm_runtime_enable);\n     \n      ## include/linux/pm_runtime.h ##\n     @@ include/linux/pm_runtime.h: static inline void pm_runtime_disable(struct device *dev)\n    -  * Allow the runtime PM autosuspend mechanism to be used for @dev whenever\n    -  * requested (or \"autosuspend\" will be handled as direct runtime-suspend for\n    -  * it).\n    -+ *\n    + \t__pm_runtime_disable(dev, true);\n    + }\n    + \n    ++/**\n     + * NOTE: It\u0027s important to undo this with pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend()\n     + * at driver exit time unless your driver initially enabled pm_runtime\n     + * with devm_pm_runtime_enable() (which handles it for you).\n    -  */\n    ++ */\n      static inline void pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(struct device *dev)\n      {\n    + \t__pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(dev, true);\n```\n\nPlease refer to the contribution guidelines for details:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/README.md",
